WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.590
Now that Marvel Studios has confirmed that
Mahershala Ali will lead the Blade reboot

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:09.490
as Eric Brooks, artists and Photoshop experts
have created edits and illustrations imagining

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.720
what Ali could look like as the Daywalker.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.600
Here's a glimpse at some of the best.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:19.400
Using a poster of Mahershala Ali as the devious
Vector in Alita: Battle Angel, artist @mizuriofficial

00:00:19.409 --> 00:00:23.029
whipped up a cool edit of what the actor might
look like as Blade.

00:00:23.029 --> 00:00:27.480
Ali's Blade rocks black sunglasses and an
all-black suit, holding a massive sword ready

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:31.080
to slice and dice any vampires that come his
way.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:36.160
Also inspired by Mahershala Ali's performance
as Vector in Alita: Battle Angel, popular

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:40.720
digital artist and Photoshop master @Bosslogic
created an edit of what the Oscar-winner could

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:41.950
look like as Blade.

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:46.179
We can't tell what's more impressive: Bosslogic's
work, or that he created the edit five months

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:48.379
before Ali was announced as the new Blade.

00:00:48.379 --> 00:00:49.379
"Are you from the future?”

00:00:49.379 --> 00:00:50.670
“Well, he is.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:51.670
I'm not.”

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:53.400
“That's brilliant.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.360
Do they still have sandwiches there?"

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:59.120
When Marvel announced that a Blade reboot
was happening with Ali taking the lead as

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:03.920
Eric Brooks, Goldie Arver got to work illustrating
some seriously stunning concept art and shared

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:05.520
the results on her Instagram.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:09.610
Her illustrations depict Ali's Blade in a
full costume and with fangs, with a close-up

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:12.890
shot of him looking head-on at the camera
with red sunglasses.

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:16.600
Arver also shared a standalone version of
the front-facing illustration.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:22.590
In digital artist Montajes Asgaya's rendition
of Mahershala Ali's Blade, the character wears

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:26.670
his hair in a hi-top fade style that shows
off his head and neck tattoos, and holds his

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:29.240
weapon of choice gracefully in his hand.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:34.160
Against a deep red background, Blade looks
determined, time-hardened, and totally badass.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.240
“Ooh, ooooh, so exciting."

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:42.310
Omar Rios imagines that when Mahershala Ali
takes the blade to become the new Eric Brooks,

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:44.310
he'll get more than just his hands dirty.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:49.340
On his Instagram page @ozone719, Rios shared
a full-color and a black-and-white illustration

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:54.040
that shows Ali's Blade with multiple weapons
and a bulletproof vest that's covered in blood.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:59.670
Another person who predicted Marvel Studios
would cast Mahershala Ali as the famous Daywalker

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:02.350
was artist and illustrator Masood Tahir.

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:06.640
Uploading his striking original artwork on
his Instagram @mastahgram, Tahir shared an

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:10.610
eye-catching black-and-red-soaked illustration
of what Ali could look like when he makes

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:12.810
his Marvel Cinematic Universe debut.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:14.890
It's bound to put a smile on anyone's face.

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:18.800
[Blade smiles, then stops smiling.]

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:24.000
On his Instagram account @ultraraw26, Yadvender
Singh Rana made a piece of art that shows

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:28.520
Ali's Blade with an intense look on his face,
staring someone down from behind red-lensed

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:31.250
glasses as he reaches for the weapon on his
back.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.600
If that doesn't scream Blade, we don't know
what does.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:39.160
Artist Camille Vialet imagined that Mahershala
Ali's iteration of Blade will hold nothing

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.020
back in the forthcoming reboot.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:45.870
On her Instagram account, @cvialet_art, Vialet
shared her vision of the actor in the role:

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:50.569
kneeling on the ground, wearing a smug smirk
on his face as enemies aim their weapons directly

00:02:50.569 --> 00:02:52.280
at his chest, shoulder, and leg.

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:56.260
It's easy to imagine him getting ready to
devastate his enemies with a perfect one liner.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:57.490
You know, something like…

00:02:57.490 --> 00:03:01.280
"Some motherf---ers are always trying to ice
skate uphill."

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:06.319
Empire Design art director Olly Gibbs took
an oh-so-sleek approach with his artwork depicting

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:09.570
what Mahershala Ali might look like as Blade
on his Twitter.

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:13.350
Against a bright red background, Ali's Blade
looks dramatically to his right while resting

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.400
his gun against his shoulder and neck.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:20.880
Jackson Caspersz created a beautiful illustration
of Mahershala Ali as Blade, while a number

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.630
of enemies lurk in the background.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:26.430
The picture appears to depict a scene just
seconds before an awesome rooftop vampire

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:29.880
fight scene, one where the vampires learn
a very important lesson:

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:33.720
"There are worse things out tonight than vampires.”

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.080
“Like what?”

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:36.560
“Like me."

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:43.150
Artist @apexform was so impressed with Ali's
casting as Blade that they created an ultra-cool

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:47.459
edit in which Ali's version of Blade has red
eyes, two blades on his back, and loads of

00:03:47.459 --> 00:03:48.459
tattoos.

00:03:48.459 --> 00:03:51.870
Whatever Ali's Blade looks like in the upcoming
film, one thing's for sure.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:55.510
"You tell him it's open season on all suckheads."

